  "question": {
    "text": "If the area bounded by the curve <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> and the line <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;sq. units,&nbsp;then the value of&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3.2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0041_e176866ad34d.png\" style=\"width:2.56972in;height:1.38806in\" /><br />The curves are <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math><br />The intersection points are <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> where<br /><math><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2,6</mn></math><br />i.e. <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,12</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>6,12</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br />Thus, the required area is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo stretchy=\"true\">&#8747;</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>6</mn></munderover><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>12</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>-</mo><msubsup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msubsup></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>216</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>36</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>208</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>128</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>48</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>208</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;sq. units"
  }
